---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AnnualCalculator from '../components/AnnualCalculator.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<Layout 
    title="Annual Mileage Calculator | Estimate Yearly Driving 2026"
    description="Free annual mileage calculator. Estimate your yearly driving miles accurately for insurance quotes, car leases, and vehicle depreciation tracking."
    keywords="annual mileage calculator, yearly mileage calculator, car lease mileage calculator, commute mileage calculator"
>
    <section class="hero">
        <h1>ANNUAL ESTIMATOR</h1>
        
        <div class="instruction-box">
            <p>Project your yearly driving total based on your daily commute and weekend habits. Car leases typically come with strict mileage limits. Use this tool to accurately project your yearly total and avoid costly overage penalties.</p>
        </div>

        <AnnualCalculator />
    </section>

    <section class="seo-section">
        <div class="seo-content">
            <h2>Accurate Annual Mileage Estimator</h2>
            <p>Are you looking to buy a new car, sign a lease, or get a new auto insurance quote? Knowing your annual mileage is essential. Car leases typically come with strict mileage limits (e.g., 10,000 or 12,000 miles per year). Our <strong>annual mileage calculator</strong> takes the guesswork out of the equation.</p>
            
            <h3>How It Works</h3>
            <p>By entering your average daily commute (round trip), the number of days you work per week, and an estimate of your weekend driving, our tool can accurately project your yearly total. This helps you avoid costly overage penalties on leases or under-insuring your vehicle.</p>
            
            <h3>Why is Annual Mileage Important?</h3>
            <p>Insurance companies use your annual mileage to determine your risk level and premium. Less driving generally means lower premiums. Furthermore, tracking your annual mileage helps estimate the depreciation of your vehicle's value over time.</p>

            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What is the average annual mileage for a driver?</h3>
                <p>In the United States, the average driver covers roughly 13,500 to 14,000 miles per year. However, this varies significantly by age group, gender, and state (rural vs. urban).</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What happens if I go over my lease mileage?</h3>
                <p>If you exceed the mileage limit on a car lease, you will be charged a per-mile penalty at the end of the lease term. This fee usually ranges from 15 to 30 cents per excess mile, which can add up to thousands of dollars.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
